#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059674 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059502 :question/id #uuid "539b5b86-7b31-52c9-be04-e80d6799b68a" :question/math-academy-id "e-3623" :question/problem "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of $$\n\\displaystyle 3\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\dfrac {\\pi}{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n2\\sin \\left(\\dfrac {\\pi} {8} \\right) \\cos \\left(\\dfrac {\\pi} {8} \\right) = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the above by $\\dfrac 1 2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n3 \\, {\\color{black}\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)} } = 3 \\left( \\color{black} \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\right) = \\dfrac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c898bbf-004c-5905-a0a0-761adefc8bd8" :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696408 :question-generator/id #uuid "033d31e2-570f-5f71-ab72-e30bfee16bde" :question-generator/script "generators/7c/7c68ce8fa05e08763f0dd38109622e6a47c87dd80f933c918b34ab78cabe4415/generator.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060249 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33f0f137-c430-5061-9aba-b7129465682e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288376} {:answer/id #uuid "35864b6e-3160-54c7-bb0e-bbc1a3db4cf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288392} {:answer/id #uuid "4b2e4678-898e-5968-8e8e-f42eee7f8c22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288553} {:answer/id #uuid "9b91da1b-cbc8-5cbe-9932-fdd206c48a34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289077} {:answer/id #uuid "dc2818c1-253d-5758-83e4-f0b3910f6f07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289497}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35864b6e-3160-54c7-bb0e-bbc1a3db4cf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288392} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b668a88-94da-5c15-92cb-0b1782d6eb86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290033}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9f5ad5b9-cf75-5c20-a9c5-6e5d15578fe2" :question/math-academy-id "q-24788" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $$\n\\displaystyle {\\left(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\right)}^{2}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we expand the parenthesis and use the Pythagorean identity.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\left(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\right)}^{2} & ={\\sin }^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)+{\\cos }^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right) \\\\  & =\\left[{\\sin }^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)+{\\cos }^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\right]-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right) \\\\  & =1-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right) & =1-\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\left(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\right)}^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060398 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd1ce8ba-4050-5bed-a376-b476bdf4207e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059011} {:answer/id #uuid "e815df7e-44a2-531e-be91-ba623436da44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059012} {:answer/id #uuid "32a0df22-7caa-5ed4-9102-d4266036ef41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059013} {:answer/id #uuid "6