ulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "22b1843d-4007-53d9-ab88-b98d3616888d" :question/math-academy-id "q-120036" :question/problem "Find the exact value of ${(\\operatorname{sin}({165}^{∘})-\\operatorname{cos}({165}^{∘}))}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we expand the parenthesis and use the Pythagorean identity.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\operatorname{sin}({165}^{∘})-\\operatorname{cos}({165}^{∘}))}^{2} & ={sin}^{2}({165}^{∘})-2\\operatorname{sin}({165}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}({165}^{∘})+{cos}^{2}({165}^{∘}) \\\\  & =[{sin}^{2}({165}^{∘})+{cos}^{2}({165}^{∘})]-2\\operatorname{sin}({165}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}({165}^{∘}) \\\\  & =1-2\\operatorname{sin}({165}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}({165}^{∘})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{cos}x=\\operatorname{sin}2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={165}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}({165}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}({165}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}(2\\cdot {165}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}({330}^{∘}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain\n\n$$\n1-2\\operatorname{sin}({165}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}({165}^{∘})=1-\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{(\\operatorname{sin}({165}^{∘})+\\operatorname{cos}({165}^{∘}))}^{2}=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253634 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a688a79-b89b-5a35-859e-9149fddd7243" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250780} {:answer/id #uuid "707de248-a804-5090-bb48-1024b7978c05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251472} {:answer/id #uuid "88d27f46-cee8-5aaf-a22c-9714e10049d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251708} {:answer/id #uuid "8d7b26e1-8cd7-5f50-a6e4-a5249bb1359c" :a